From {{inh|nl|dum|wit}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|*wit}}, from {{inh|nl|gmw-pro|*hwīt}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*hwittaz}}. The geminate is unexpected as the usual {{cog|gem-pro|-}} form is {{m|gem-pro|*hwītaz}}, from {{cog|ine-pro|*ḱweytos||shine; bright}}. 

The geminate is sometimes explained as being the result of {{w|Kluge's law}}, thus from a pre-Germanic {{m|gem-pro|*kweyd-nos}}.

