# The ability to make a decision based on the combination of knowledge, experience, and intuitive understanding.
# {{lb|en|theology}} The ability to know and apply [[spiritual]] [[truth]]s.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1652|author=[[w:Thomas Vaughan (philosopher)|Eugenius Philalethes]]|title=The Fame and Confeſſion of the Fraternity of…the Roſie Croſs|sectionurl=http://books.google.co.uk/books?id=SzYCAAAAQAAJ&pg=PT2&dq=%22%C5%BFhe+foreknoweth+Signs+and+Wonders%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=xH4CT4XGC4nb8QOXyOiRCA&ved=0CF0Q6AEwBA#v=onepage&q=%22%C5%BFhe%20foreknoweth%20Signs%20and%20Wonders%22&f=false|section=pages 1-2 of the preface
|passage='''Wiſdom'''…is to a man an infinite Treaſure, for ſhe is the Breath of the Power of God, and a pure Influence that floweth from the Glory of the Almighty; ſhe is the Brightneſs of Eternal Light, and an undefiled Mirror of the Majeſty of God, and an Image of his Goodneſs; ſhe teacheth us Soberneſs and Prudence, Righteouſneſs and Strength; ſhe underſtands the Subtilty of words, and Solution of dark ſentences; ſhe foreknoweth Signs and Wonders, and what ſhall happen in time to come.}}
# {{lb|en|rare}} A group of [[wombat|wombats]].
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|author=Tony Cooper|title=Ebay is Unfair!|newsgroup=rec.collecting.coins|url=https://groups.google.com/g/rec.collecting.coins/c/tvEk3n4Z1iw/m/KxcsBWTi5zEJ|accessdate=2022-09-05|date=Apr 16, 2007|passage=It would also be difficult to get to the bottom line accurately if a '''wisdom''' of wombats ate your working papers. Both scenarios are equal in probability.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017|author=Peggy A. Wheeler|title=The Splendid and Extraordinary Life of Beautimus Potamus|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=HGKXDwAAQBAJ&pg=PT10&dq=%22wisdom+of+wombats%22&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwiShc3u8fz5AhX9kYkEHeybBLMQ6AF6BAgIEAI#v=onepage&q=%22wisdom%20of%20wombats%22&f=false|passage=Beautimus strolled to the river for her morning bath. She looked one direction, then the other to search the landscape for anything or anybody who might offer a clue as to what could be coming her way. She passed a pond where a congregation of alligators and a '''wisdom''' of wombats engaged in a heated argument over economics. Nothing unusual in that.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2020|author=Graham Jackson|title=The7th Victim|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=-OvcDwAAQBAJ&pg=PA160&dq=%22wisdoms+of+wombats%22&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwji7ez18vz5AhUylIkEHaVgCWMQ6AF6BAgCEAI#v=onepage&q&f=false|page=160|passage=''Banyule'' means ''hill'', another voice whispers from the swamp, and as I turn to ask a question I see kangaroos lying in the shade of a low tree by the shining water. Yes, the water has returned, along with giant earth-eating creatures boring holes far below, linking '''wisdoms''' of wombats with wastelands of Winthers.}}
# {{lb|en|rare}} A group of [[owl|owls]].
#: {{syn|en|parliament}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1974|author=Margery Weiner|title=Answering Any Questions: How to Set Up an Information Office|publisher=Newton Abbot : David and Charles [for] the "Daily Telegraph"
|text=What he expected to find I cannot imagine , unless it was a '''wisdom''' of owls. What he did see and hear were telephones ringing, assistants answering them, getting up from their seats to take a book or a card from a file, returning{{nb...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2016|author=Gary Barwin|title=Yiddish for Pirates: A Novel|isbn=9780345815514|page=91
|text=All of us, whether we gather into a wisp of snipes, a '''wisdom''' of owls, a wing of plovers, or remain like a single regretful priest on his knees before his God, we are one and it is not for us to decide another's fate.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|colloquial}} {{ellipsis of|en|wisdom tooth}}.
